<title>YUGOSLAVIA: YUGOSLAV JULY OIL IMPORTS DROP VS JUNE.</title>
<headline>YUGOSLAV JULY OIL IMPORTS DROP VS JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the</p>
<p>following energy statistics.</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL IMPORTS		JULY	 JUNE    JULY 96</p>
<p> Tonnes			   91,158    129,370     59,798</p>
<p> Million USD			  14	   19	    8</p>
<p>OIL DERIVATIVES IMPORTS</p>
<p> Tonnes			   24,785     29,517     19,483</p>
<p> Million USD			   8	    8	    6</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS IMPORTS</p>
<p> Tonnes				 --	   --	  397</p>
<p> Million USD			  --	   --	   --</p>
<p>NOTES -- Cumulative January-July crude imports stood at 1.232 million tonnes and were worth $203 million, compared to 222,564 tonnes worth $35 million in the January-July 1996 period.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-July oil derivatives imports amounted to 330,818 million tonnes worth $87 million, compared to 815,608 tonnes worth $170 million in the same seven-month period 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-July natural gas imports in the first seven months of the year stood at 529,730 tonnes and were worth $79 million.</p>
<p>Figures refer to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
</text>
